  "prefLabel": "Env-A 3203.31 Maximum heat input capacity",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 3203.31 “Maximum heat input capacity” means the ability of a budget source to combust a stated maximum amount of fuel on a steady-state basis, as determined by the physical design and characteristics of the unit, and is expressed in millions of British thermal units (MMBtu) per unit of time.\n\nSource. #11001, eff 1-1-16; ss by #14632, eff 6-25-26, EXPIRES: 6-25-36 (formerly Env-A 3203.33)",
